<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">314 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Luceria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucera, ancient Luceria, is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on a hill overlooking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tavoliere-delle-puglie">Tavoliere</a> plain. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> founded a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> colony there in 314 BCE during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samnite-wars">Samnite Wars</a>. In the 1220s Emperor Frederick II settled Muslims from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in the town, which remained a Muslim community until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-naples">Charles II of Naples</a> destroyed it in 1300. Its great Angevin fortress still stands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lucera.jpg" alt="Lucera" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vonvikken · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_comune_of_Lucera_(province_of_Foggia,_region_Apulia,_Italy).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
